Fix the cutover wrapper's self-contradictory readiness gate.

`cutover_runtime_ready` proves three services at once:

  wait_for_cutover_asterisk_ready   -> requires verify_no_tcp_listener 8088
  wait_for_coordinator_ready
  wait_for_nginx_ready              -> requires nginx listening on 0.0.0.0:8088

The first demands port 8088 be empty; the third demands nginx be on it. Both
run inside the same call, so once the cutover starts nginx the function can
never return 0. That is why the cutover reached the real switch, replaced every
config, started all three services, and then failed the closing re-sample with
`cutover_listener_set_not_exact` and rolled back. The gate is unsatisfiable by
construction, not by any property of this host.

The check exists to prove Asterisk has vacated the plain-HTTP port, and the
bundle already carries the predicate that says exactly that -- the wrapper uses
`verify_no_tcp_listener_owned_by 8088 asterisk` in its own state vocabulary at
line 1363. That is the correction.

Nothing is weakened. `verify_exact_tcp_listener` asserts a listener count of
exactly one, at the exact local address, owned by the expected process name and
MainPID, so `wait_for_nginx_ready` alone still proves 8088 is held by nginx and
by nothing else. The relaxed predicate only stops Asterisk's proof from being
falsified by nginx doing its job.

  before: c36aa4343f8fda11ac1a9c445de70a1c659590e7690fe2019647da3e1593f63f
  after:  98e9261e6cf3ed66e1bedea187a2a91b418afc2ceb7355241125eddaf9fc16c5

Applied to /usr/local/sbin/fanum-pbx-coordinator-deploy, which the cutover
workflow pins by digest; both pins are rolled forward in the same commit.

--- a/fanum-pbx-coordinator-deploy
+++ b/fanum-pbx-coordinator-deploy
@@ -1507,7 +1507,7 @@
     main_pid="$(systemctl show asterisk.service --property=MainPID --value 2>/dev/null)"
     if systemctl is-active --quiet asterisk.service \
       && verify_exact_tcp_listener 8089 127.0.0.1:8089 "$main_pid" asterisk \
-      && verify_no_tcp_listener 8088; then
+      && verify_no_tcp_listener_owned_by 8088 asterisk; then
       return 0
     fi
     wait_count=$((wait_count + 1))
